==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|frank|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹæŋkli/}}
* {{hyph|en|frank|ly}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-frankly.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# {{senseid|en|candidly}} In a [[frank]] or [[candid]] manner, especially in a way that may seem [[too]] [[open]], excessively [[honest]], or slightly [[blunt]].
#: {{collocation|en|speak '''frankly'''}}
#: {{ux|en|He spoke '''frankly''' about the economy.}}
#* {{RQ:Vance Outsider|page=382|column=2|passage=She was '''frankly''' disappointed. For some reason she had expected to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven, burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp.}}
# {{senseid|en|sentence adverb}} {{lb|en|sentence adverb}} [[in truth|In truth]], [[to tell the truth]].
#: ''Most of what they said was, '''frankly''', a pack of lies.''
#* {{quote-av|en|title=Gone with the Wind|year=1939|actor=Clark Gable|role=Rhett Butler|url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankly,_my_dear,_I_don%27t_give_a_damn|passage='''Frankly''', my dear, I don't give a damn.}}
# {{senseid|en|obviously}} {{lb|en|science|medicine}} To a degree large enough as to be plainly {{l|en|evident}}.
#: {{cot|en|evidently|obviously|apparently|macroscopically|grossly|id5=greatly|greatly|palpably}}
#: {{collocation|en|'''frankly''' septic}}
#: {{collocation|en|'''frankly''' psychotic}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|manner}} {{l|en|candidly}}, {{l|en|forthcomingly}}, {{l|en|honestly}}, {{l|en|truthfully}}; {{l|en|bluntly}}; see also [[Thesaurus:honestly]]
* {{sense|sentence adverb}} {{l|en|as a matter of fact}}, {{l|en|to be frank}}, {{l|en|truth to tell}}; see also [[Thesaurus:actually]]

